00:49:04.040 --> 00:49:05.820
And remember, the vector in
question is w.

00:49:05.820 --> 00:49:06.920
x is not a vector.

00:49:06.920 --> 00:49:07.860
Yeah?

00:49:07.860 --> 00:49:11.160
You can do just put the
transpose inside.

00:49:11.160 --> 00:49:15.820
So w transpose x transpose.
and then the X transpose X.

00:49:17.200 --> 00:49:17.840
Yeah,

00:49:17.840 --> 00:49:20.840
and that's like the.

00:49:21.460 --> 00:49:22.760
Yeah, exactly.

00:49:22.760 --> 00:49:23.180
Remember,

00:49:23.180 --> 00:49:26.380
X W transpose is the same as W
transpose X transpose.

00:49:26.380 --> 00:49:28.980
But now, like we did before in
that earlier example,

00:49:28.980 --> 00:49:32.080
I have my vector on the outside,
which is what I want.

00:49:32.080 --> 00:49:35.620
W transpose times box times W.

00:49:35.620 --> 00:49:38.120
Again, remember, the vector we
are taking the gradient with

00:49:38.120 --> 00:49:40.160
respect to is W.

00:49:40.160 --> 00:49:41.520
W is the vector here.

00:49:41.520 --> 00:49:42.640
So that part's good.
OK,

00:49:42.640 --> 00:49:47.890
what about what we have going on
in the middle?

00:49:48.060 --> 00:49:52.800
I want to write this like
something involving w.

00:49:57.540 --> 00:49:58.540
Firstly,

00:49:59.380 --> 00:50:02.060
and maybe we'll go to the side
here,

00:50:02.060 --> 00:50:07.740
the terms we have are y
transpose xw

00:50:07.740 --> 00:50:11.160
and xw transpose y.

00:50:12.200 --> 00:50:15.640
Those are the terms involved.
They're just both negated.

00:50:15.640 --> 00:50:17.220
Do we agree that those are the
same thing?

00:50:17.220 --> 00:50:21.220
They're both the dot product of
y with x w.

00:50:21.220 --> 00:50:22.720
Do we agree?

00:50:22.720 --> 00:50:23.720
OK.
So those are the same.

00:50:37.500 --> 00:50:41.880
But none of these forms really
look like anything related to

00:50:41.880 --> 00:50:43.080
our big three rule.

00:50:43.080 --> 00:50:45.260
Because our big three rule, the
one that relates to a dot

00:50:45.260 --> 00:50:46.260
product,

00:50:46.260 --> 00:50:49.740
involves a dot product of w with
something.

00:50:49.740 --> 00:50:53.780
But right now, these look like
dot products of xw with y.

00:50:53.780 --> 00:50:58.760
So how can I massage one of
these expressions

00:50:58.760 --> 00:51:02.180
to look like the dot product of
xw,

00:51:02.180 --> 00:51:05.860
or sorry, of the dot product of
w with something?

00:51:05.860 --> 00:51:07.200
Let me put it this way.

00:51:07.200 --> 00:51:10.120
We just established that y
transpose xw

00:51:10.120 --> 00:51:14.620
is equal to xw transpose y.

00:51:14.860 --> 00:51:19.360
What does that also equal to?

00:51:20.240 --> 00:51:24.740
What does this also equal to?

00:51:25.260 --> 00:51:26.260
Yeah?

00:51:26.480 --> 00:51:29.000
w transpose x transpose y.

00:51:29.000 --> 00:51:31.380
w transpose x transpose y.

00:51:31.380 --> 00:51:35.880
And now what does this look
like?

00:51:39.000 --> 00:51:41.250
This looks like,

00:51:41.680 --> 00:51:46.180
does it look like the dot
product of w with something?

00:51:49.680 --> 00:51:51.880
It does.
It's the dot product of w with

00:51:51.880 --> 00:51:52.880
what?

00:51:53.700 --> 00:51:55.300
Yeah, x transpose y,

00:51:55.300 --> 00:51:59.800
right? This is indeed the same
thing as w dot x transpose y.

00:52:01.060 --> 00:52:02.060
So,

00:52:03.320 --> 00:52:05.660
if I go back here,

00:52:05.660 --> 00:52:09.460
Because these two terms are both
the same,

00:52:09.460 --> 00:52:14.140
I can write a 2 followed by any
